From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:10:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: let a join run while the regulatory domain
 settles

The roam's station came up on the new channel, then the join stopped with
-ECANCELED just after mac80211 sent the authentication. That is the regulatory
stop. mac80211's disconnect for the new authentication makes cfg80211 restore
its settings, through the world domain and back to the country, and that
takes RTNL as soon as the authentication request returns. The new lifetime
was in use by then, so it ended.

While a join is starting, let the domain settle: the firmware keeps the
domain it has, and an update that matches clears the wait. A change still
unsettled when the data phase starts ends the lifetime there, as a change
during a lifetime did before.

Part of the Wi-Fi daily-use plan, phase 4.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c     |  3 +++
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac-priv.h |  2 +-
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c     | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c
index 296e9387a..c751590a4 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c
@@ -1719,6 +1719,9 @@ int mt6797_mac_join_release_channel(struct mt6797_mac *mac)
 
 	if (!mac->ccmp_pm_connected || !mac->ccmp_pm_credit_ns)
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+	/* The regulatory change did not settle during the join. */
+	if (mac->reg_pending)
+		return -ECANCELED;
 	if (!mac->join_channel_granted || mac->join_channel_released ||
 	    mac->join_data_phase || mac->join_page_debt || mac->join_credit_pending)
 		return -EBUSY;
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac-priv.h b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac-priv.h
index 9f057d2d0..3a0d7a942 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac-priv.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac-priv.h
@@ -438,7 +438,7 @@ struct mt6797_mac {
 	char alpha2[2];
 	/* The domain and power the firmware last accepted. */
 	struct mt6797_regulatory_payloads reg_sent;
-	bool reg_sent_valid;
+	bool reg_sent_valid, reg_pending;
 	unsigned int sequence;
 	/* The first command sequence of lifetime 1, where a recycle restarts. */
 	unsigned int sequence_base;
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
index 1a8999fc1..0ab135df1 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
@@ -458,9 +458,22 @@ static void mt6797_mac_regulatory(struct wiphy *wiphy,
 		memcpy(saved, mac->alpha2, 2);
 		mt6797_mac_set_alpha2(mac, request->alpha2);
 		if (!mt6797_mac_policy(mac, &policy) &&
-		    !memcmp(&policy, &mac->reg_sent, sizeof(policy)))
+		    !memcmp(&policy, &mac->reg_sent, sizeof(policy))) {
+			mac->reg_pending = false;
 			goto out;
+		}
 		memcpy(mac->alpha2, saved, 2);
+		/* A disconnect makes cfg80211 pass through the world domain and
+		 * back to the country. For a roam that lands just after the
+		 * join starts, so let the join run while it settles; the
+		 * firmware keeps its domain. A change still unsettled when the
+		 * data phase starts ends the lifetime there.
+		 */
+		if (mac->join_running && !mac->join_retired && !mac->join_cleanup_done &&
+		    !mac->join_data_phase && mac->join_scan_ready) {
+			mac->reg_pending = true;
+			goto out;
+		}
 	}
 	if (mt6797_mac_join_regulatory_stop(mac, &discard, &internal))
 		goto out;
-- 
2.43.0

